logo: keep the boot logo data alive after init memory is freed

The logo bitmaps are emitted __initdata/__initconst and logo.c marks
them unusable at late_initcall_sync (logos_freed). On the Pi 3 the
vc4/DPI pipeline needs several deferred-probe rounds (spi-gpio ->
ili9806e -> component bind), so vc4drmfb only registers at ~6s -
while init memory is freed at ~2.6s (bench dmesg, v2.2.0-fcc53ba).
When fbcon re-takes-over on the real framebuffer, fb_find_logo()
returns NULL and the Boompi logo silently never draws. (The earlier
takeover at 0.8s draws onto the firmware simplefb, which the dark
DPI panel never scans out.)

Keep the generated logo in .data/.rodata permanently (~70KB - noise
on these boxes) and drop the logos_freed latch, so a late fbcon
takeover can still find and draw it.

--- a/drivers/video/logo/logo.c
+++ b/drivers/video/logo/logo.c
@@ -27,15 +27,9 @@
  * Use late_init to mark the logos as freed to prevent any further use.
  */
 
-static bool logos_freed;
-
-static int __init fb_logo_late_init(void)
-{
-	logos_freed = true;
-	return 0;
-}
-
-late_initcall_sync(fb_logo_late_init);
+/* Boompi: logos are no longer __initdata (see pnmtologo.c); they
+ * survive free_initmem so a late-probing DRM fbdev (vc4 behind a
+ * deferred-probed DPI panel) can still draw the boot logo. */
 
 /* logo's are marked __initdata. Use __ref to tell
  * modpost that it is intended that this function uses data
@@ -45,7 +39,7 @@
 {
 	const struct linux_logo *logo = NULL;
 
-	if (nologo || logos_freed)
+	if (nologo)
 		return NULL;
 
 	if (depth >= 1) {
